  The Qodana plugin holds an embedded copy, because the 'intellij.qodana' main module uses SARIF and
  Qodana extension point signatures pass SARIF values across a plugin boundary. A plugin that passes a
  SARIF value to Qodana must reuse that copy: depend on 'intellij.qodana.sarif', the wrapper in the
  'jetbrains' namespace, and register no copy of its own.

  The DFA Analysis plugin holds a copy that is not embedded, for its content module
  'intellij.dfa.analysis.rml.utils'. No SARIF value crosses the OpenGrep to Qodana boundary, so the RML
  side stays free of the Qodana plugin. A copy that is not embedded keeps its own classloader, so only a
  module that names it can see it.

  Register no third copy. Two copies that one module can reach put the same class in two classloaders
  and raise a LinkageError.
  See QD-15883 and build/decisions/0005-a-library-copy-belongs-to-the-plugin-that-owns-its-api.md.
-->
